<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 27 June, from 1743 to 2007.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1743 CE <span class="tih-ago">283 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George II leads his army to victory at Dettingen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a>, an allied army under George II beat the French in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. It was the last time a reigning British monarch commanded troops in battle.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/carthage" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carthage.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1844 CE <span class="tih-ago">182 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mormon founder Joseph Smith is killed by a mob</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Militiamen stormed the jail in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, where Smith and his brother Hyrum were held, and shot them dead. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigham-young">Brigham Young</a> later led most of his followers west to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1905 CE <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sailors mutiny aboard the battleship Potemkin</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Crew of the Russian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea-fleet">Black Sea Fleet</a> battleship rose against their officers after a dispute over rotten meat. The mutiny became a symbol of the 1905 Revolution, later immortalised by Eisenstein.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1950 CE <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">UN Security Council calls on members to defend South Korea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Resolution 83 recommended that members help <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a> repel the North's attack. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> was boycotting the Council and could not veto it.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2007 CE <span class="tih-ago">19 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gordon Brown succeeds Tony Blair as Prime Minister</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After ten years as Chancellor, Gordon Brown became Prime Minister. His premiership was dominated by the global financial crisis of 2008.</p></div></li></ol>
